From 7432bb3cc5105f6705b2ea753155383b15cde2de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:27:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 114/116] MAS local: turn the window only once the guest has
 taken the rotation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A click on the rotate button while Android was still booting turned the
window, but `settings put system user_rotation` failed with no guest to
take it and was not tried again: from then on the window and the picture
were a quarter turn apart.

- The button is disabled, saying 旋转屏幕：等安卓开机完成 on hover, until the
  boot's setting of the display rotation has gone through and Android has
  booted (the boot script now also waits for sys.boot_completed=1). A boot
  sync that fails (adb lost, a boot past its limit) is tried again after
  5 s.
- A click sets the guest's display rotation first and turns the window
  only once the guest has taken it; a guest that does not leaves both as
  they were (and says so in the log). One click at a time.

Test: aemu-ui-lean-window_unittests (57), aemu-ui-safe-shutdown_unittests
(17).

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#225

Change-Id: Ic14ad0c8ec74ae7b1f37ef70dc0b3f224c8bf9c3
